298 0 obj
<<
/Title (Why Do the Leverage Models Win?)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 447 0 R
/Next 26 0 R
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Title (Answer:  no. A monthly-refit EGARCH\(1,1\) gives the best QLIKE; no learned model beats the leverage GARCH family where it matters. Nuance:  the LSTM ranks third, ahead of plain GARCH, and is statistically tied with the winner; LSTM and XGBoost take the best RMSE and MAE. Leverage matters:  on a window with two asymmetric crashes, EGARCH and GJR significantly beat plain GARCH. Main lesson:  a leak-free walk-forward harness and the choice of metric matter more than model complexity. Future work:  intraday realized variance, extra inputs like the VIX, and multi-asset training.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 26 0 R
>>
endobj
